A||||4||86SE||Finally raced that SHO!!||||3||
Z||000000||86SE||04-12-2001||12:33 AM||||After all this time I have been wantin to race this 1993 or somethin Ford Taurus SHO 5-speed with Yamaha head kits.  <P>We set up, they count 1-2-3!!  I take off like a bat outta hell. Take it to 5500 in first, already have a half-car legnth on him, take it to about 6000 in second.  Im doin about 80.  Now im 1 car legnth ahead of him.  Hit third gear and I could hear him commin up on me.  He passed me when I was doin 95, and only gained about 2 cars on me.  I had it maxed out in final gear, engine turnin at about 5600 RPM, speedo pegged about 600 revz ago.<P>He may have beat me after a mile, but I for sure killed him in the 1/4 mile, 1/2 mile, and 0-60-95.  I must say, I was very impressed with my Fiero after that!  Everyone told me I would get killed by him, but I don't think I did.<P>Thats my race story for this week.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||3
Z||000001||sqoach||04-12-2001||12:44 AM||||Sounds like a pretty good run. Those SHO's are very quick and got some good top end power. I was driving my brother's 89 5 spd back from OKC today and some guy in a low-rider Grand Am with fat wheels was trying to race me. Enough said  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily overheating)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||04-12-2001||12:51 AM||||I have raced a few SHO's , there are a couple in our autocross club , haven't lost yet ..<P>In an unrelated story...<P>I had the oppertunity to ride in a 2 million ..yes 2 million dollar mercury sable. The car was built by alcan , all aluminum , had an SHO drivetrain , big brakes , really nice car , you could tell the weight difference (600lbs) when you started tossing the car around..and no ..a stock-ish fiero would not beat it ... the motor had a chip , higher compression ..really a work of art. <P>good kill<P>JM ||||reg||1
